 ```
 
+A server that requires authentication can be given `headers`, which are sent with every request to that server (discovery, invocations and lifecycle notifications) and to no other host:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "toolset_server",
+  "server_url": "http://127.0.0.1:3010",
+  "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer <token>" }
+}
+```
+
+Headers are stored in plain text in the config file, so keep it private. They are not applied to session migration requests.
+
 Installed servers appear in the same file as `toolset_command` entries, which spawn the server binary on demand and read its port from stdout. [MCP servers](./configuring-mcp.md) use the `mcp_server` and `http_mcp_server` entry types in the same `tool_sets` array.
